I think I tracked this down.  Someone probably already fixed this, but 
it appears to be a bug in the vanilla 3.4.3 Nethack.  I was able to 
recreate it.  I've created a simple patch:

http://www.bobbydurrettdba.com/uploads/dropcoinaltar.patch

When a priest is killed above an altar and its gold is dropped the gold 
object keeps its flag bknown set to false.  When a player drops gold on 
an altar, the gold object's bknown flag gets set to true and the two 
piles of gold don't stack because bknown is one of the flags that have 
to be the same for two objects to stack.

The fix is to prevent the flag from being set to true when a player 
drops gold since Nethack doesn't track b/u/c status for gold.

It was fun sifting through the code and messing with gdb to find the bug.

